local_user tables get filled even if there was an error with the dp_authentication users table.


Env Secrets - dont keep secrets in application.properties instead it should be a env var on your machine
Token Expiration - Make sure your JWT expiration times are reasonable (15-60 minutes for access tokens)
Refresh Token Rotation - Consider implementing refresh token rotation for better security
Rate Limiting - Add rate limiting on login/registration endpoints
HTTPS Enforcement - Ensure all environments use HTTPS
Token Revocation - Consider how to handle token revocation if needed

Environment Configuration - Move secrets to environment variables
Logging - Add more security-focused logging (failed logins, etc.)
Error Handling - Ensure no sensitive data leaks in error responses
Refresh Token Implementation - Fully implement refresh token flow
Account Lockout - Implement temporary account lockout after failed attempts
Email Verification - Add email verification for registrations

Device Management - Track and manage active sessions/devices
Security Headers - Add security headers (HSTS, Content-Security-Policy)
Audit Logging - Log security-related events